[[Menu: Complete liquidDX11 Liquid Glass UI remake with frosted blur panels, diagonal specular rim highlights, and 5 glass material presets (Subtle, Default, Frost, Vivid, Deep) in Appearance]],
[[Chrome: Top-center Dynamic Island (expands on hover with latency & command hint), macOS Traffic Light window controls, sliding liquid-glass sidebar selection pill, bottom magnifying macOS dock, glass profile popover, and Ctrl+K Command Palette]]
,[[Widgets: Spring-animated pill switches with liquid velocity stretch, bouncy knob sliders, and click-ripple glass buttons]]}},{'v5.32.6',{[[Menu: Higher-resolution (512x512) sidebar logo with a refreshed cache download]],
[[Keybinds: Mouse 3 (middle click), Mouse 4, and Mouse 5 (side mouse buttons) can now be bound everywhere as MB3, MB4, and MB5 (including Hold/Toggle modes, Menu Toggle/Panic keys, Teleports, Vehicle Jump, Automations, Keybind List, and saved configs)]]
}},{'v5.32.5',{[[Settings: Reverted the Server Browser back to the v5.32.1 behavior]]}},{'v5.32.4',{
[[Settings: Server Browser now detects reserved/matchmade games whose main place is a 1-player launcher (like FLATS) instead of showing fake 1/1 servers, and Server Hop re-enters matchmaking via the main place]]}},{'v5.32.3',{
[[Settings: Server Browser now falls back to Asc / limit=50 / full-included queries and the game's root PlaceId (for sub-places) so it stops falsely saying 'No other servers found' when servers are listed on the website]]}},{'v5.32.2',{
[[Settings: Server Browser now fetches 1 page at a time to stay under Roblox's 3-requests/min limit and caches the server list on disk (Understanding_servers.json) so reloads and rate limits keep your server list usable]]}},{'v5.32.1',{
[[Players: Spectate now works across the whole map like Freecam even when a player's character is streamed out, and no longer turns off or snaps back in games that reset the camera every half second]]}},{'v5.32',{
[[Visuals: dragging Name, Distance, Weapon or the Health bar in the ESP Preview now follows your mouse live instead of jumping when you let go]],
[[Menu: smoother animations and transitions, a one-click clear button in the search bar, and faster tab switching]],[[Performance: faster ESP, Radar and Overlays with less frame work when many players or objects are on screen]],
[[Reliability: cleaner reset of movement, camera, vehicle and character settings when you respawn or unload the menu]]}},{'v5.31.2',{
[[Vehicle: Cruise Control and Autopilot hold their speed across vehicles with wheel motors, movers, nested car models, and scripts that brake on RenderStepped / Stepped]],
[[Vehicle: Cruise Control remembers the speed you had before letting go of W to click the toggle, and has full power in cars that brake hard by themselves]],
[[Vehicle: Autopilot keeps its speed through gentle turns and skips route waypoints that have fallen behind the car]],[[Vehicle: the Status box shows how hard the game slows the car while Cruise Control or Autopilot drives]]}},{'v5.31.1',{
[[Vehicle: Cruise Control really holds your speed now, uphill and downhill, also in cars that brake by themselves when you let go]],
[[Vehicle: Autopilot works without a destination: it drives around, keeps to the road it is on and takes a turning now and then]],[[Vehicle: the Status box shows the speed Cruise Control holds and what Autopilot is doing]]}},{'v5.31',{
[[New Wardrobe tab: save the avatars you like and try them on (only you see it)]],[[Save a player's outfit from the Players tab, or anyone's by username]],
[[Buy opens Roblox's own avatar window for a saved outfit; Links copies the items' catalog links]],[[Try Catalog Item puts one item or bundle on top of what you wear, from its ID or link]]}},{'v5.30',{
[[Vehicle: Cruise Control holds your speed; braking switches it off]],[[Vehicle: Auto Dodge steers into the nearest gap when a car or wall is in the way, with a slider for how close it cuts]],
[[Vehicle: Autopilot drives to a saved place, or to anything in the Teleports list (the Walk button reads Drive while you sit in a car)]],'Vehicle: Flying Car - the car hovers, E goes up and Q down',
'Vehicle: Drive on Water and Wall Driving'}},{'v5.29',{[[New Automations tab: build your own rules, 'when this happens, do that']],
[[When: health drops below a percent, an item or NPC appears, a player joins, you respawn, a key, a timer, the menu starts, you sit in a vehicle]],
[[Then: switch a feature on or off, teleport to a saved place, go back, load a config, show a notification]],[[Each rule can be for this game or every game, has a wait time, and is kept between sessions]],
[[The panic key pauses your rules, so nothing switches back on by itself]]}},{'v5.28.1',{[[Teleports: an item you picked up no longer stays in the list (tools in a backpack or in someone's hand, switched-off prompts)]],
[[Teleports: a row whose thing is gone leaves the list within a couple of seconds]]}},{'v5.28',{[[New Teleports tab: your saved places, NPCs and items in one list you can search and filter]],
[[Go teleports you there, Walk goes on foot; same-named NPCs and items are one row that goes to the nearest]],[[Items are dropped tools and things you can use or click; the search also finds any object by name]],
[[Back to Where I Was returns you to the spot before your last teleport]],[[Right-click a saved place (or the back button) to give it a key]],[[Saved Teleports moved here from the World tab: your saved places are kept]]}},{'v5.27.1',{
[[Home: a What's New section shows what changed in the newest versions, with a button for the older ones]]}},{'v5.27',{[[Vehicle: Drift - the car slides through corners; give it a hold key for a handbrake-style drift button]],
[[Drift sliders: how long it slides, how fast it swings round, the widest angle, and power to keep the slide going]]}},{'v5.26.1',{
[[Update notice: the check can no longer be answered with an old, saved reply, so a new version is noticed within 5 minutes]],[[Settings > Script: Check for Updates looks for a new version right away]]}},{'v5.26',{
[[New Vehicle tab: works on any car, boat or kart you drive yourself]],[[Speed Boost with top speed and acceleration, Nitro (give it a hold key) and Instant Brake]],
[[Turn Assist, Extra Grip, Downforce, Air Control, Anti-Flip and a Flip Vehicle button]],[[Vehicle Jump on its own key (H until you change it), jump height, air jumps and vehicle gravity]],
[[Speedometer you can drag anywhere, in studs per second, km/h or mph]]}},{'v5.25.1',{'Home: Join the Discord now sits right under your favourites','Home: the music player is gone'}},{'v5.25',{
[[Join the Discord: new button at the bottom of the Home tab (copies the invite)]],[[Welcome card the first time you run the menu, with the basics]],
[[The menu tells you once which features your executor can't run, so nothing quietly does nothing]]}},{'v5.24',{
[[New watermark in the menu's own style: separate cells for FPS, ping and the time; FPS and ping turn yellow or red when they get bad]],[[Choose what the watermark shows: Watermark FPS, Watermark Ping, Watermark Clock (Visuals > Overlays)]]
,[[New Keybind List: real rows with a dot and a key cap, a header that counts what is on, and it grows to fit long names]],[[Only Active Keybinds: the list only shows the features that are on]]}},{'v5.23.5',{
[[The loader now always gets the newest version straight after a release (it could give the previous one for a few minutes)]]}},{'v5.23.4',{
[[ESP preview: no longer zoomed in - it zooms out until your whole avatar fits (hair, crowns, tails), with the box around the body like in the game]],'ESP preview: a label you drag follows the pointer again'}},{'v5.23.3',{
[[ESP preview: the box now fits your avatar the way it does in the game (hats, wings and floating effects no longer shrink the avatar)]],[[ESP preview: the skeleton follows your avatar's own body instead of a fixed stick figure]],
[[ESP preview: labels on the left or right are no longer cut off - the box makes room for them]]}},{'v5.23.2',{[[More clean-up: changing animation packs no longer leaves old animations loaded]],
[[Browsing the emote Library for a long time no longer keeps growing memory]],[[Turning X-Ray or Performance Mode off, and turning the Loud Sound Limiter on, no longer hitch on big maps]],
[[Invisible recovers by itself if it fails in a game (the toggle used to stay stuck)]]}},{'v5.23.1',{[[Big clean-up for long sessions: less memory used over time and less work every frame]],
[[ESP is lighter in full servers (skeleton, boxes and labels only update what changed)]],[[X-Ray, Remove Invisible Walls and Performance Mode always put the map back, and no longer freeze big maps when switched]],
[[Emotes keep working after hundreds of plays in one life; My Emotes and the Library are smoother with big collections]],[[Fixed: Chat Spam or the Jerk Tool could keep running after turning them off or reloading]],
[[Fixed: Anti-Void could get stuck putting you back every frame on low maps]],[[Fixed: turning Invisible off right after on could lose your character]],
